/ A row of the list, like a mail in a list of mails: the dot of an unread
  notification stands in a column of its own at the left, so the titles line
  up, read or not. On a phone the rows are the cells of a grouped list. The
  separator starts after the dot, and the last row has none.
li class='group/row' id=dom_id(notification)
  = link_to notification_path(notification),
            class: 'flex items-stretch gap-2 pl-2 lg:rounded-lg active:bg-fill-strong pointer-fine:hover:bg-fill focus-ring-inset',
            data: Ui::TurboModal::Component.link_data do
    span.flex.w-3.shrink-0.justify-center.pt-4.5
      - if unread?
        span.size-2.5.rounded-full.bg-indigo-500.dark:bg-indigo-400 aria-hidden='true'
    div class='flex min-w-0 flex-1 items-center gap-3 border-b border-line py-3 pr-4 group-last/row:border-b-0'
      .min-w-0.flex-1
        div class=['line-clamp-2 text-headline leading-snug text-fg', ('font-semibold' if unread?)]
          - if unread?
            span.sr-only = "#{t('.unread')}: "
          = title
        time.mt-0.5.block.text-sm.text-muted = formatted_published_at
      = icon 'chevron-right', class: 'text-sm text-faint lg:pointer-fine:hidden'
